<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><img class="phero-bg" src="/assets/img/photos/insurance-paperwork.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/insurance-paperwork-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/insurance-paperwork.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span>Claim wordbook</nav><p class="tag">Reference</p><h1>Property Claim Wordbook: Terms Defined</h1><p class="lede">40 terms you’ll see in Rhode Island policies, estimates and appraisal awards, defined in plain English.</p></div></section><div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><div class="filter"><label for="gloss-filter">Search the wordbook</label><input id="gloss-filter" type="search" placeholder="Try “deductible” or “umpire”" autocomplete="off"><p class="hint" data-gloss-count>40 terms</p></div><div class="az"><a href="#g-A">A</a><a href="#g-C">C</a><a href="#g-D">D</a><a href="#g-E">E</a><a href="#g-F">F</a><a href="#g-H">H</a><a href="#g-I">I</a><a href="#g-L">L</a><a href="#g-M">M</a><a href="#g-N">N</a><a href="#g-O">O</a><a href="#g-P">P</a><a href="#g-R">R</a><a href="#g-S">S</a><a href="#g-U">U</a><a href="#g-W">W</a><a href="#g-X">X</a></div><dl class="glossary"><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-A">Actual cash value (ACV)</dt><dd>Replacement cost minus depreciation. Many policies pay ACV first and the rest after repairs.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Additional living expense (ALE)</dt><dd>Coverage for extra costs of living elsewhere while your home is uninhabitable after a covered loss.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Amount of loss</dt><dd>The dollar value of a covered loss. It’s what appraisal decides.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Appraisal award</dt><dd>The written decision signed by two of the three panel members that sets the amount of loss.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Appraisal provision</dt><dd>The policy condition that lets either side demand appraisal when they disagree on the amount of loss.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Appraiser</dt><dd>A competent, disinterested person named by each side to value the loss.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-C">Causation</dt><dd>What caused the damage, such as wind versus flood. Usually a coverage question, not an appraisal question.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Coinsurance</dt><dd>A commercial policy condition that can reduce payment if the property is insured below a required percentage of its value.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Coverage A</dt><dd>Dwelling coverage: the limit for the house itself on a homeowner policy.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Coverage B</dt><dd>Other structures coverage: detached garages, sheds, fences and similar.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-D">Declarations page</dt><dd>The summary page of your policy listing coverages, limits and deductibles.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Depreciation</dt><dd>A reduction in value for age and condition, used to calculate actual cash value.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Disinterested</dt><dd>Without a personal stake in the outcome. Policies require appraisers to be disinterested.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Dwelling form</dt><dd>A policy form often used for rental properties, which can differ from a standard homeowner form.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-E">Endorsement</dt><dd>A form attached to the policy that adds, removes or changes coverage.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-F">FAIR Plan</dt><dd>A state-established insurer of last resort. Rhode Island’s FAIR Plan covers properties that can’t get coverage elsewhere.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Flood exclusion</dt><dd>The homeowner policy provision excluding damage from flood and surface water, including storm surge.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-H">Hurricane deductible</dt><dd>A deductible, usually a percentage of Coverage A, that applies when a storm meets the policy’s hurricane trigger.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-I">Ice dam</dt><dd>A ridge of ice at the eaves that traps meltwater, which can back up under shingles and leak inside.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-L">Line item</dt><dd>A single entry on an estimate with a description, quantity, unit and price.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Loss of rents</dt><dd>Coverage for rental income lost while a rented unit can’t be lived in after a covered loss.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-M">Matching</dt><dd>Whether replacement materials can reasonably match the undamaged remainder of siding, roofing or flooring.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Mitigation</dt><dd>Reasonable steps to prevent further damage after a loss, such as tarping or drying.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-N">Named storm</dt><dd>A tropical storm or hurricane named by the National Hurricane Center, a common hurricane-deductible trigger.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>NFIP</dt><dd>The National Flood Insurance Program, which writes most residential flood policies in the U.S.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Nor’easter</dt><dd>A coastal storm with strong northeast winds, common in Rhode Island from fall through spring.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-O">Ordinance or law coverage</dt><dd>Coverage for added costs of meeting current building codes during repairs.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Overhead and profit (O&amp;P)</dt><dd>A general contractor’s charges for managing a job with several trades, often 10% and 10%.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-P">Proof of loss</dt><dd>A sworn statement of the amount claimed, often due within a set time after the insurer requests it.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-R">Recoverable depreciation</dt><dd>Held-back depreciation the policy pays once repairs or replacement are completed.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Replacement cost value (RCV)</dt><dd>The cost to repair or replace with materials of like kind and quality, without deducting depreciation.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-S">Scope</dt><dd>The full list of repairs needed, before pricing.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Square</dt><dd>A roofing measurement equal to 100 square feet of roof surface.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Steep charge</dt><dd>An estimate line adding labor for working on steep roofs.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Storm surge</dt><dd>Seawater pushed ashore by a storm. Treated as flood under homeowner policies.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Suit limitation</dt><dd>The policy condition limiting how long you have to sue the insurer, often counted from the date of loss.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt>Supplement</dt><dd>A request to add missing or underpriced items to a claim after the first estimate.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-U">Umpire</dt><dd>The neutral third member of an appraisal panel who decides items the appraisers can’t agree on.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-W">Wind-driven rain</dt><dd>Rain forced through openings by wind. Coverage depends on whether wind first created an opening.</dd></div><div class="g-item"><dt id="g-X">Xactimate</dt><dd>Estimating software widely used by insurers and contractors to price property repairs.</dd></div></dl></article><aside class="side"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-t">Talk it through</h2><p>A free first conversation. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="box-phone" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn ink" href="/request-a-claim-review/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-t">Learn</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/the-appraisal-sequence/">The appraisal sequence<svg class="ic" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/policyholder-questions/">Policyholder questions<svg class="ic" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/claim-wordbook/" aria-current="page">Claim wordbook<svg class="ic" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/claim-notebook/">Claim notebook<svg class="ic" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li></ul></div></aside></div>
</main>
